  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Norec, FK Norway, personnell exchange</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Organic farming promotion programme supports young people&apos;s participation in organic agriculture as a tool for sustainable development. Parmath Samaj Sevi Sansthan in India has expertise on water management, which Integrated Village Development Service wishes to adopt. IVDS specializes in developing community based farming projects, which PSSS wishes to integrate into their programming. During the first two rounds of the project, former participants have developed the concept of a farmer business school and obtained government funding for the initiative. The partners use the exchange to help the Farmer&apos;s business school concept be more sustainable. 
The overall aim of the project is to make organic farming appealing to young people, and therefore dissuade youth from urban migration in the two countries.</narrative>
  </description>
